    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A ritardando and an a tempo (docs/plan/prompts/73)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A gradual tempo change is written as where it arrives and how far it takes" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// to get there: `tempo 1/4 = 72 to 48 over 2/1;` says the quarter slows from" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// 72 to 48 across two whole notes. What happens in between is a shape, and" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the shape is in the score rather than in any one performance of it." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The interpolation is linear in *seconds per beat*, not in beats per minute." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// That is not a rounding decision: interpolating bpm makes each beat's" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// duration a reciprocal, so the elapsed time stops being rational and the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// exactness the whole temporal model rests on is gone. Interpolating duration" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// keeps every intermediate value exact — and it is also what an orchestra" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// plays when it is told to slow down evenly, so the representable answer and" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the musical one are the same answer." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The last marking is a word with no number: *poco rit.* over a whole note" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// prints, and moves no clock. Which is the point — the page can say more than" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the map does, and a design that fused them could not." },
